From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:02:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: PLAYPORT_VK_BUDGET_MB caps the heap's memory budget

KosmicKrisp reports one device-local heap the size of Metal's
recommended working set (8 GiB on a 12 GB iPhone) and a
VK_EXT_memory_budget budget of 90% of what the process may still
allocate plus what Metal already holds (about 6 GiB at a game's start).
Both are far above the video budget Playport's memory plan leaves the
guest beside its RAM (1,536 MiB on that phone, what DXMT reports): DXVK
over KosmicKrisp told games 8 GiB of dedicated video memory and a 6 GiB
budget, and sized its own residency to that.

When PLAYPORT_VK_BUDGET_MB is 256 or more, cap heap 0's budget at that
many MiB; the host app sets it from the plan only for a title that opts
in. The heap's size stays Metal's working set: an application may size
pools or caches from the heap size, and shrinking it below what the
device can hold would change what it may allocate, not just what it is
advised to use; DXVK's own option (dxgi.maxDeviceMemory) already clamps
the dedicated memory DXGI reports. Unset, the driver is unchanged. One
line on stderr says the cap and the heap size.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-15-vulkan-clamp.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.h |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
index b7be613..0efbd14 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
@@ -30,6 +30,8 @@
 #include "vk_drm_syncobj.h"
 #include "vk_shader_module.h"
 
+#include <inttypes.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
 #if DETECT_OS_APPLE
@@ -1088,8 +1090,14 @@ kk_get_sysmem_heap_budget(struct kk_physical_device *pdev)
    /* Budget is calculated using the default Mesa logic, based on available
     * system memory. Available memory is reduced to 90% to avoid thrashing. */
    const float available_percent = 0.9f;
-   return vk_physical_device_heap_budget_from_system(
+   uint64_t budget = vk_physical_device_heap_budget_from_system(
       &pdev->vk, available_percent, heap_size, used);
+
+   /* The host app's video budget, when it asks for one: the heap's size stays
+    * Metal's working set, only the budget is capped. */
+   if (pdev->heap_budget_cap_B && budget > pdev->heap_budget_cap_B)
+      budget = pdev->heap_budget_cap_B;
+   return budget;
 }
 
 static void
@@ -1250,6 +1258,16 @@ kk_enumerate_physical_devices(struct vk_instance *_instance)
       goto fail_disk_cache;
    }
 
+   /* PLAYPORT_VK_BUDGET_MB (256 MiB to 1 TiB): the host app's video budget,
+    * set only when the title opts in. */
+   int64_t budget_cap_MB = debug_get_num_option("PLAYPORT_VK_BUDGET_MB", 0);
+   if (budget_cap_MB >= 256 && budget_cap_MB <= (INT64_C(1) << 20)) {
+      pdev->heap_budget_cap_B = (uint64_t)budget_cap_MB << 20;
+      fprintf(stderr, "[kk-memory] heap 0: size %" PRIu64 " MiB, budget capped "
+              "at %" PRId64 " MiB (PLAYPORT_VK_BUDGET_MB)\n",
+              sysmem_size_B >> 20, budget_cap_MB);
+   }
+
    uint32_t sysmem_heap_idx = pdev->mem_heap_count++;
    pdev->mem_heaps[sysmem_heap_idx] = (struct kk_memory_heap){
       .size = sysmem_size_B,
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.h b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.h
index 9d815cf..b4f141a 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.h
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.h
@@ -76,6 +76,9 @@ struct kk_physical_device {
    VkMemoryType mem_types[3];
    uint8_t mem_heap_count;
    uint8_t mem_type_count;
+   /* PLAYPORT_VK_BUDGET_MB in bytes: the most the device-local heap's
+    * VK_EXT_memory_budget budget reports; 0 for no cap. */
+   uint64_t heap_budget_cap_B;
 
    // Emulated binary sync type
    struct vk_sync_binary_type sync_binary_type;
